        eb1.WithTitle("PROLOGUE : : O8 / O3 / 2O26");
        eb1.WithDescription("Footsteps. Hurriedly. First on metal, then on concrete. Then, it stills some. At the end of the day, people walk home from work and rush to and fro to return to their families.\n\n\nThat is what one mother was doing on a day like any other. She'd get home late at night, call for her son, and cook meals with him. From the beginning, it'd only been the two of them; they didn't see each other much these days—both of them were busy, but they still made time for one another like this. \n\n\nEven if it was small, the mother thought it was enough.\n\n\n“… I should really check the air index, it's been foggy the past couple of days,” the mother thought out loud to herself as she stepped inside her house and discarded her belongings near the door. “Haven't I said that a lot? I really should do it tonight.”\n\n\nShe gave one look around before coughing roughly, the sound muffled by the dense environment. “And it's even… worse in here…? Did he try to cook something? * * * * !” The mother called for her son.\n\n\nWhile her son helped her with food, she did most of the work. He was unable to do much by himself recently, so the thought of him trying both warmed her heart and worried her. She wondered why, too; there were always leftovers in the fridge—these days, he'd only eat half of his food. Something about dieting?\n\n\nShe moved closer to the stairs.\n\n\n\" * * * * !” The mother called for her son again, though it scratched at her throat.\n\n\nStill nothing. The house had two floors, so it made sense that he wouldn't hear her. Maybe he had headphones in. She furrowed her brows in what was beginning to be frustration. She went up the creaking stairs, stopping right below the second-to-last step.\n\n\n\" * * * * ! Come down!” She called once more, though the words were hard to make out; the atmosphere on the upper level made her head feel woozy—as if there were something in the air beyond simple fog…\n\n\n. . . And still, nothing from her son. Concern was in her mind for a second, until it was replaced with anger. \n\n\nShe stormed up the rest of the stairs and down the hall to her son's room, gripping the handle before throwing it open. The mother stormed over to her son, who seemed to be under the blankets. She dragged them off his body and grabbed his arm quickly, her mouth ready to spew reprimands… Yet, she paused. Something was wrong.\n");
        eb1.WithColor(0x393c45);
        
        eb2.WithDescription("His skin was cold.\n\n\nNot cold like it is in the winter months. Not cold like it is when he turns up the fan too much and leaves it on accidentally.\n\n\nHis skin is brittle in a way that living skin shouldn't be, like leather.\n\n\nThe bed was caked in sweat, and he was unmoving. She shook his arm, and his entire body moved with it. She heard the dense clink of a pill bottle underneath him, shaken by the stiff movement. \n\n\nA pill bottle, but no pills. They'd been refilled that Monday.\n\n\nThe mother stood there, hand still on her son's impossibly stiff body. She couldn't move; it was as if the world itself stopped moving.\n\n\n*He was going to graduate soon. *\n\n\nNo, this was a dream, just a terrible dream. Soon, she'd wake up and peer into his room to see him playing games like usual.\n\n\n* He would have gone to college. *\n\n\nMaybe she passed out because of the smoke in the area. It was getting worse. Why hadn't she ever checked the air index?!\n\n\n*He would have found someone to love. *\n\n\nHe's joking, isn't he? He'll open his eyes now, hug her, and say he 'got her!' He'd laugh, he'd smile, he'd *breathe*—\n\n\n*Found happiness where she couldn't. *\n\n\nHer face was drenched in tears. Why? Her son was alive. \n\n\nShe could have started crying because it was so foggy. Maybe she was crying because she couldn't see, or because her eyes were open too long. No, maybe it was because of the deafening silence of her home. Her son was alive, and he just had to breathe. Despite all evidence, he just needed to—\n\n\nA mother’s wail pierced the silence as the inability to keep the truth from reality crept in. It didn't break through the fog. The air was too dense. \n\n\nShe started crying because she missed his innocent smile and little hands. Her lips trembled because she missed his old, bulky red backpack. She sobbed because she didn't want him to grow up. She heaved because he got into Kyoto University, and because she didn't want to see him leave home. She couldn’t stop crying because she didn't want to let go. She didn't want to let go.\n\n\nHer only son was gone.\n\n\nGone, and never coming back.\n\n\nShe screamed until her throat was raw.\n\n\n\" * * * * ! \"\n.\n.\n.\n");
        eb2.WithColor(0x202228);
        
        eb3.WithDescription("“And unfortunately, they aren't the only ones.” The man from the JJOC spoke, finally having adjusted his computer's camera to look the General in the eyes. \"One hundred fifty and counting, probably more than that; all concentrated in that area. Murders, suicides, the like. It's completely unprecedented, and no one can figure out why!”\n\n\nThe General picked up the laptop sitting on the desk and walked over to the map in her office, her trusty planning assistant. “You said this was in... Chiyoda, is that right? Why there…?”\n\n\n“Yes, it's completely unheard of. The local police can't make heads or tails of it. You know your mission, Kamikawa. See to it that it is completed.”\n\n\nThe General, Kamikawa, nods her head. “Yes, sir.”\n\n\n“You are dismissed.”\n\n\nAs she shut her laptop and wrote more about the task at hand, she spoke into the microphone at her side, which broadcast her voice throughout the staff building. “All CO, report to the upper-level command center within 15 minutes. Plans have changed.”\n.\n.\n.\n\n\n[ click . . ]");
        eb3.WithColor(0x6c5931);
        
        eb4.WithDescription("“Today is the 3rd of August, 2026 . . . \" [ click. ]\n\n\n“Have you ever wanted to have clearer skin? Now y— \" [ click. ]\n\n\n“Ugh! When are they going to play *our* songs on one of those stations?” Tagai Ryōga, an idol known for his loud and boisterous personality, shouted into the open-seating area of the Recreation and Training Facility, clicking rapidly through the channels on his radio. He and two other people were sitting either on couches or, for whatever reason, *behind* the couches.\n\n\n“Uh, maybe when it's not 10 A.M. on a Monday?...” Tagai's bunkmate and close friend, Himura Kazumi, responded, affixing their headphones to their microphone case; they both were in the building to *train*, but since they got here, all they've done is talk. Himura tosses Tagai's sword to him—which, thankfully, he catches—and starts to walk to a room labeled TO3, or Training Three.\n\n\n“… Are we supposed to be using our radios for that?” Kandou Kaede, another idol, popped her head out from behind the couch; it seems she was looking out the windows in the area in thought. \n\n“Hey!! I use them for our normal stuff too! But, you know, it's a radio!! \" Tagai waved his hands in the air, laughing slightly. “Why not use it for radio purposes?”\n\n\n\"Hey… Get in here, or I'm starting without you two.” \n\n\n“Got it!” \n\n\n“Sorry!...”\n\n\nAs the two idols ran to catch up and start their training regimen, two more people came into the main foyer.");
        eb4.WithColor(0x842513);
        
        eb5.WithDescription("“Aaaand this is the Recreation and Training Facility, or for short, the RTF. We do … practically everything here, it's one of our biggest buildings!” A red-headed idol, the bright and ever-passionate Wu Hongye, motions excitedly towards the now-empty room. “People come in here to train for fighting *and* performance, and I know a couple of groups spend hours making entire choreographies in here on their off-time!”\n\n\nThe person she's showing around is a new *Jieikan Kōhosei*, someone new to the force, and they seem to be taking in the sights. The walls in the main foyer are made primarily of glass, and the floor is carpeted. Upon taking a look inside the actual training rooms, though, everything's made of brick, with floors of stone, tile, or a thin carpet-like material. The Kōhosei is in awe. “It's really cool…”\n\n\n“I know, right? That's not all, though—we're only one building into our tour!” Wu took their arm and led them back outside.\n\n\nThe actual base grounds weren't anything special; it was a green, grassy area with paths made of coral-colored stone. The grass itself was a dark, muted color, with trees, taller than long, scattered along the paths and behind the buildings. There were a few signs explaining where to go, and numbers on every structure's front wall. Worn benches were staggered alongside some of the paths, where enlisted could be spotted chatting, gossiping, or sparring with one another.\n\n\n“And over there are the two Administrative Headquarters,\" Wu points out to two buildings near the front of base, one white and tall, and one grey and stocky. \"The white one is where the NCOs and higher sleep, as well as… uh, where they plan the big stuff that eventually becomes our missions! The grey one behind it is sort of similar, but it's where they do important *relations stuff* with other military branches.”\n\n\nThe group begins to walk away from the base's entrance, passing homes and stores, where people can be seen doing menial tasks like picking up trash and walking out of said stores with snacks. \n\n\n\"Here's the place where you'll get your headphones and sword after your training. It's a small classroom area with a few doors outside!! It leads to a sort of track area..? It's a bit bare, so people don't typically go over there unless they have to.\" Wu leads the new Kōhosei to a white building. Peering in, there are a few rooms to the left and right of the entrance, followed by an upstairs and a door in the middle that leads to the track area Wu was talking about. Next to it are two other buildings: one labeled 'Motorpool' and the other, 'Armory', which store armored vehicles and weapons/tools, respectively. Inside, both places looked the same: beige brick walls, a stone floor, but obviously, the things they held were different. \n\n\n\"Aaand finally ~\" Wu does a pose that motions the newly enlisted's focus to the last two buildings in the impromptu tour she brought them on. “The Personnel Barracks and the Canteen!! A.K.A., where we sleep and where we eat; they're connected by a tunnel, so people like to go that way when it's hot! No WiFi down there, though. Breakfast and Dinner are at 6:20 AM and 6:20 PM. Make sure to wake up when the horn plays at 6:00 AM, or you're toast. Warning you now because it's *lou*—”");
        eb5.WithColor(0xb23e3e);
        
        eb6.WithDescription("[ BEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEP! ]");
        eb6.WithColor(0xc29936);
        
        eb7.WithDescription("The phone in Wu's pocket goes off, and she nearly jumps 3 to 5 feet in the air. She fishes it out of her skirt pocket (with some difficulty) and peeks at it… Then her face beams with excitement. “Hey!! I'm being called on a mission!” \n\n\n\nShe points to an area past some bushes, \"That's the 'SPOT', it's just a place we hang,\" Then, to a building in the opposite direction, \"That's the ceremony hall! It's used for church and rank ups,\" Then, to a busier looking place just west of the Barracks, \"And that's the place everyone gets their accessories. Y'know, charms, trinkets!! Okay-okay! I gotta go, call me if 'ya need anything!\" And with that, she zoomed off into the Barracks building, holding up a peace sign.\n\n\n.\n.\n.\n");
        eb7.WithColor(0xb23e3e);
        
        eb8.WithDescription("“Can you believe it? We've barely even gotten comfortable with the place, yet we're already on an important mission!” A voice rang out from the Enlisted barracks building.\n\n“Well, I have to believe it...\" Another voice sounded, a lot more hesitant this time.\n\n\nPast their room, many other idols had gotten the notification and were nearly ready to prepare and practice before meeting their squadron commandant in the center of the base. Some were just returning from a mission and groaned at the thought of being away from base for another week, some were in the canteen buttering up the cooks so they could get food after missing breakfast, some were in the recreational building in the middle of training, and screamed *way* too loud when they saw their mission.\n\n\nGrabbing their swords and noise-canceling headsets off the walls, the idols rush out to prepare for their mission in their Parade Dress with their performance outfits tucked securely in a bag at their side. Some grabbed their instruments; some grabbed their *Kanai-anzen* talismans for protection; some grabbed their friends and shook the nervousness out of them.\n\n\nThis is how idols acted right before being sent on a mission: screaming into microphones, practicing difficult dances or dodges, and hyping up nervous people. They screamed mantras at one another, leaving no room for fear or doubts in their hearts, no matter how unseasoned they may be against the foe they'll be going up against.\n\n\nNo one knows what it is, yet, but they do know one thing: \n\n\n*If they show any amount of weakness, they're done for.*\n\n\nThey have to be strong for their peers, their family, and the good of the nation. If they have even a *modicum* of worry or wrongness in their hearts, they're a target.\n");
        eb8.WithColor(0x842513);
        
        eb9.WithDescription("Once the time comes for them to set out, a loud, short, sharp alarm rings throughout the base, and each idol assigned to the mission begins their venture to the center of the base.\n\n\nFor those in the Barracks, all they had to do was walk northward towards the center. Everyone else had to run, or at least jog, to get to the center on time, as the other buildings were much farther than they had any right to be; in between or behind residential housing for any husbands, wives, or children of the Enlisted.\n\n\nEventually, though, everyone arrived to see Azusawa Muko, a *Santō Sa* ranked Commissioned Officer; she would be the one to both debrief them further and command them throughout their mission. The area had no seating, so all Enlisted were standing in order—a 5-by-4 formation. They stood there quietly, arms held behind their backs as Azusawa began to speak.\n\n\n“Good afternoon, idols.”\n\n\n“Good afternoon, ma'am!” The many Enlisted shouted in rehearsed quickness. They were used to it by this point. \n\n\n“You all know what you are to do, I am sure. I'll go over it once more to make sure no misunderstandings happen out there,” Azusawa spoke, walking around the small crowd in front of her, checking them carefully to see if they have everything they require.\n\n\nThe commissioned officer continued speaking. “There's been a sudden, great amount of casualties and suicides in the Chiyoda area, specifically around this area—Awajicho. We'll need to do some reconnaissance in the area, and, in the case that there's any reason we need to arm ourselves, we will,\" she announced and nodded slightly, grabbing her sheathed sword and affixing it to her side with red rope.\n\n\n“We move out in T-minus 30 minutes. Say a quick parting message to the family you have here, if they are here.”\n\n\nThus, a group of 15 *Nitō Shi* and 5 *Jieikan Kōhosei* began preparing to head out. Some said goodbye to their families and friends, some with tears, some with smiles and \"You can do it!\"s; and less than 30 minutes later, they were out and on the road in armored trucks to Aoyama Park.");
        eb9.WithColor(0x6c5931);
        eb9.WithFooter("To be continued . . .");
        
        var channel = command.Channel as SocketThreadChannel;
